NAME
    rom - hash library games, verify dump integrity, and find duplicates

SYNOPSIS
    rom hash [-r] [--comparable] <path>...
    rom check [-r] <path>...
    rom dups [<console>]
    rom wait [rom<n>]

DESCRIPTION
    Read-only library inspection tool of the emusen.library module. Each
    <path> is a file or folder relative to the library root
    (AppSettings.RomDirectory), using '/' separators (for example, snes or
    "psx/Rayman (USA).cue"). Directories require '-r' and are walked using
    the library scanner's rules (cue sheets represent their tracks, .m3u
    playlists represent their discs, and '/' with '-r' scans the whole
    library). Directly named files are read unconditionally.

    rom never writes to, renames, or removes files in the library. Data
    lines go to standard output for piping; diagnostics and summaries go
    to standard error.

    'hash' prints one line per file (or per track for cue sheets, named
    <sheet>#<nn>):

        <crc32> <md5> <sha1> <size> <name>

    Hashes are lowercase hex, separated by single spaces so <name> is the
    remainder of the line. With '--comparable', each game prints one line
    normalized to its console's comparable form:
      - Cartridges strip console headers (NES iNES header, 512-byte SNES
        copier header) or normalize byte order (N64 big-endian).
      - Zips hash the playable image inside after verifying zip CRC-32.
      - Discs (cue/bin, CHD, ISO, raw track) hash sectors read through
        EmuSen's disc reader (2,352-byte CD sectors from track 1 index 01
        to lead-out, or 2,048-byte DVD user sectors).

    'check' prints '<name>: ok' or '<name>: <check>: <reason>; ...' using
    structural checks that do not require an external DAT catalogue:
        size     Unreadable, empty, or non-integral sector size.
        sheet    Malformed cue sheet, missing track/disc, or broken m3u.
        archive  Corrupt zip directory, empty zip, or CRC-32 mismatch.
        chd      chdman verify failure or unreadable hunk/sector. If the
                 pinned chdman binary is absent, prints one warning and
                 checks CHDs with EmuSen's reader alone.

    'dups' prints groups of games sharing identical comparable CRC-32,
    MD5, SHA-1, and size, separated by blank lines. A package and the
    library files it claims (such as a '--beside' CHD and its original)
    count as one game and do not form a duplicate group.

OPTIONS
    hash [-r] [--comparable] <path>...
        Compute CRC-32, MD5, SHA-1, and size for each file or folder.

    check [-r] <path>...
        Run structural integrity checks on each file or folder.

    dups [<console>]
        Find duplicate dumps across the library or a single <console>
        (ES-DE name or system id).

    -r
        Recurse into directories named in <path> (accepted by 'hash' and
        'check').

    --comparable
        Normalize cartridges, zips, and discs to their console comparable
        form before hashing ('hash' only).

    wait [rom<n>]
        Follow a background rom job until completion.

JOBS
    Commands that exceed the ten-second foreground budget continue in the
    background as rom<n>. Use ps(1) to view progress, 'rom wait' to
    reattach, and kill(1) to stop. Stopping 'rom dups' early suppresses
    group output.

EXAMPLES
    rom hash "snes/Super Metroid (USA).sfc"
    rom hash psx/Rayman.cue
    rom hash -r --comparable snes | sort
    rom check -r / | grep -v ': ok$'
    rom dups
    rom dups psx
    rom hash -r --comparable / | sort | uniq -D -w 40

EXIT STATUS
    0   All files processed cleanly (including when 'dups' finds groups).
    1   Invalid arguments, nonexistent path, unreadable file, or one or
        more failed checks.

SEE ALSO
    chd(1), pkg(1), scrape(1), sort(1), uniq(1), ps(1), kill(1)
